# Inventions — the land's machines for sharing a weight, kept and proposed
# A design, proposed. The kept ones are already in the chapters; the proposed ones are not, and none is a line anyone says.
#>lore_land_surfaces_inventions
#:surface #!proposal
#:operation #!prime
#:fixity #!experimental
#:layer #!semantics

~<rationale>{
  A story feeds its readers by what it shows can be built. The land already invents in one direction: its best machines take a weight that one person was carrying and give it to the world, or make a cost visible so it can be shared. A counterweight in a wall, torch-lines, a slip with a line for the cause, a receipt posted where everyone can read it. More of these, in the same register, make the book more optimistic without making it sweeter: each is material, a little absurd, and honest about what it costs. Each proposed one names the sigil it would answer in the lanes, so play and story keep one physics.
}

^"kept"{
  storm_weight: "Chapter Fifteen: an iron counterweight in the wall of the parcel gate, so a gate hung for three porters can be kept by one"
  torch_lines: "Chapters One and Fourteen: the ants light a street torch to torch, and the lines run straight even on a day nobody keeps"
  damage_slip: "Chapter Fifteen: a word at the top, a line for the cause; the slip remembers the knock so nobody has to"
  posted_receipt: "Chapter Twelve: BoneWAP posts both receipts, so a gift and an apology are both written where they can be seen"
  wish_scale: "Chapter Three: pans balanced against coincidences instead of weights"
  brace_box: "Chapter Fifteen: the night school chalks two nouns, a sigil and a container on a brace-box"
}

^"proposed"{
  many_handled_tray: "A tray with a handle for everyone at the table. It gets lighter by the hand: two hands carry half each, and nobody can carry it alone because nobody is meant to. In the lanes, & confluence: a pie carried beside an escort tilts less for every hand on it"
  second_chair: "A chair folded into the side of every table in Bonk City, that opens only when someone arrives without a receipt. Stone sixteen is the second place at the table; this is how the furniture could already know. In the lanes, ^ integration: a seat binds a newcomer upward, into the table"
  thank_bell: "A small bell on the washtubs that rings once when the last plate is dry, so the work nobody watches is heard across the plaza. In the lanes, # annotation: the unseen deed gets its mark"
  backward_receipt: "A receipt that records who helped instead of who owes, kept in the same drawer as the DAMAGE slips. It answers the clerk and the Genie at once. In the lanes, $ value: what a carry gave, not what it cost"
  warm_stone: "A doorstep stone that stays warm because everyone who passes touches it. Nobody heats it; it is heated by being passed. Boof would know it by scent. In the lanes, ~ reference, a warmth that lasts a while"
  lantern_lending: "Lanterns hung at the end of every unlit street for anyone to take and leave at the next. The torch-ants approve, and correct the spacing. In the lanes, * a named thing carried"
  counterweight_library: "A lending wall of counterweights: borrow one for a heavy week, return it when the week is lighter. Kept by the porter, in his own name. In the lanes, = a lean, lent"
  lag_bench: "A bench by the field with two seats, where a hob-deer sometimes sits a beat late. Proposed as a place, not a creature: somewhere to wait that proves you were not waiting alone. In the lanes, @ perspective, the second seat"
}

!guards[
  "An invention shares a weight or makes a cost visible. None makes a problem vanish, none is bought, and none is owned by the one who made it"
  "Inventions are things, not speeches. No inventor explains one"
  "No invention touches the Egg, the figure or the hat"
  "Each stays a little absurd and exactly material: what it is made of, what it weighs, who keeps it"
]

?open[
  "Which proposed inventions, if any, may appear in a chapter, and which only in the lanes or the almanac"
  "Who in the land makes things, and is it one maker or many hands"
  "Should the many-handled tray become the lanes mechanic for escorts (tilt shared by hand) before it appears in prose"
]
